\description{
Every error this package raises from the API is a condition of class
\code{plasticdb_error}, signalled with \code{\link[rlang:abort]{rlang::abort()}}, so it can be caught by
class with \code{\link[=tryCatch]{tryCatch()}} or \code{\link[rlang:try_fetch]{rlang::try_fetch()}}. The classes mirror the
exceptions of the Python client, and a condition carries every class it
belongs to: an unknown release is both a \code{plasticdb_release_unknown} and a
\code{plasticdb_not_found}, and a merged record is a \code{plasticdb_merged} and a
\code{plasticdb_gone}.
}
